{"name":"Beef Jerky","hex":"#a25768","fetched":"2026-10-11","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"beef jerky","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Jerked meat of bovine origin."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/beef_jerky"}],"entries":[{"title":"Beef Jerky (instrumental)","blocks":[{"text":"\"Beef Jerky\" is an instrumental written by John Lennon that was released on his 1974 album Walls and Bridges and also as the B-side of the lead single from that album, the number-one hit \"Whatever Gets You thru the Night.\""}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/7/7d/Beef_Jerky_label.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Beef_Jerky_(instrumental)","wikidata":"Q108619661"},{"title":"The Jerky Boys (soundtrack)","blocks":[{"text":"The Jerky Boys (Original Motion Picture Soundtrack) is the original soundtrack album of the 1995 James Melkonian's film The Jerky Boys: The Movie. It was released on January 24, 1995, via Select/Atlantic Records."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/e/e5/Jerky_Boys_The_Movie_Soundtrack.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/The_Jerky_Boys_(soundtrack)","wikidata":"Q17006289"},{"title":"Jerky","blocks":[{"text":"Jerky is lean trimmed meat strips which are dehydrated to prevent spoilage and seasoned to varying degrees. Normally, this drying includes the addition of salt to prevent microbial growth through osmosis. The word \"jerky\" derives from the Quechua word ch'arki which means \"dried, salted meat\"."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/64/Jerky_%281%29.jpg/330px-Jerky_%281%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Jerky","wikidata":"Q1072897"},{"title":"Beef","blocks":[{"text":"Beef is the culinary name for meat from cattle. Beef can be prepared in various ways; cuts are often used for steak, which can be cooked to varying degrees of doneness, while trimmings are often ground or minced, as found in most hamburgers. Beef contains protein, iron, and vitamin B12. Along with other kinds of red meat, high consumption is associated with an increased risk of colorectal cancer and cardiovascular disease, especially when processed. Beef has a high environmental impact, being a primary driver of deforestation with the highest greenhouse gas emissions of any agricultural product."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/60/Standing-rib-roast.jpg/330px-Standing-rib-roast.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Beef","wikidata":"Q192628"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/55/Orange-marinated_beef_jerky.jpg/500px-Orange-marinated_beef_jerky.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/55/Orange-marinated_beef_jerky.jpg/1280px-Orange-marinated_beef_jerky.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/55/Orange-marinated_beef_jerky.jpg/500px-Orange-marinated_beef_jerky.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Orange-marinated beef jerky","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AOrange-marinated_beef_jerky.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/89/Meat_drying_to_make_jerky._Gandhola_Monastery%2C_Lahaul.jpg/500px-Meat_drying_to_make_jerky._Gandhola_Monastery%2C_Lahaul.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/89/Meat_drying_to_make_jerky._Gandhola_Monastery%2C_Lahaul.jpg/1280px-Meat_drying_to_make_jerky._Gandhola_Monastery%2C_Lahaul.jpg?utm_sour